  "implementation": [
    "CoreTriggerControl owns a connection-local recursive_triggers flag, its boolean PRAGMA forms and the ordinary pragma_recursive_triggers read. The setting can change in an active transaction and survives rollback/savepoint rollback. Actual resolved PRAGMA virtual tables retain DIRECTONLY behavior.",
    "Runtime admission follows the flag, while recursive preparation still compiles each active program once. Actual program entry checks 1000 frames and increments/restores triggerDepth, including a false WHEN. Structural executor fuel is separate from semantic frame depth. Native controls accept the 1000-frame workload with leaf DML and reject 1001 frames.",
    "REPLACE preparation includes reachable DELETE programs even for an empty source. A pure checked point preflight supplies its actual candidate and victims; that temporary state is discarded. Actual DELETE execution runs on the real pending state in constraint order. Its body writes count, while auxiliary deletion counts do not. A previously allocated INSERT key stays fixed despite DELETE-body insertions.",
    "PointExecutor carries an explicit complete typed UPDATE register image and its original SET footprint across victim DELETE programs. The existing RowPreparation path installs these registers without a temporary database rewrite or an expanded SET footprint. User RETURNING runs only in its actual post-deletion phase. Preparation validates a discarded counter-bound RETURNING copy while execution retains the original expressions."
  ],
  "reference_protocol": "Complete stdout/exit/first-error and independently observed persisted catalog/table/integrity contents compare with pinned SQLite 3.53.4 in rollback and WAL modes. Twelve generated recursion inputs use a new final-checkpoint seed. Every prior suite is rerun with fresh generated inputs. Tests cover both actual 1000/1001 boundaries, ordered multiple victims, defaults, frozen allocation/registers, phase/error order and immediate FK behavior. No skip, target-value filter, native production call or expected-output rewrite is used.",
  "crash_scope": "SIGKILL timing samples for recursive REPLACE INSERT/DELETE programs writing three tables, real OLD/NEW inputs, a live recursion flag and a unique index. Public Lean recovery followed by independent SQLite catalog/root-zero/rowid/schema-cookie/row/integrity checks. Complete old or new states are required. No every-syscall, power-loss or arbitrary-schedule claim.",
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned pragma.c recursive_triggers connection flags, trigger.c preparation, vdbe.c OP_Program depth checks and insert.c/update.c constraint/REPLACE row registers. Independent native comparisons determine counters, order and persistent outcomes.",
  "proof_scope": "All retained Core/file/physical and signed-counter contracts compile. New audited component laws cover read-only recursion-PRAGMA state preservation, caller frame-depth restoration, disabled replacement-program admission and successful explicit-register point context restoration. A new executable group covers actual recursion, live rollback settings and full UPDATE register retention. No global trigger/VDBE equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, RAISE, triggered UPSERT, trigger-aware ALTER, writable CTEs and wider volatile/query/constraint/error/FK combinations remain work. Native defaults are tested at the pinned trigger-depth limit; the finite suite does not exhaust recursion or REPLACE semantics.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
